# TypeScript incremental build state — regenerated by `tsc -b` on every build.
*.tsbuildinfo

# Vercel CLI link/state for this machine.
.vercel

# NOTE: `public/data/` is deliberately NOT ignored.
#
# It is generated (`npm run data:generate`) so ignoring it is the intuitive
# call — but `npm run build` never runs the generator, so nothing on Vercel can
# recreate it. Ignored, the deploy ships a `dist/` with no data and every page
# renders empty while the build stays green.
#
# Regenerate it locally and commit the diff. The generator is seeded, so a
# re-run with no code change produces no diff at all.

# Per-machine Claude Code settings.
.claude/settings.local.json
Costing model_ERA_Archive.xlsx

# The fetched copy of the assessment sheet (`npm run data:ingest -- --fetch`).
#
# Ignored because it is a byte-identical duplicate of the committed
# `List of gaps and interventions per facility.csv` at the repo root, which is
# the offline source the ingest falls back to. Committing both is 15 MB to say
# the same thing twice. Delete it and re-fetch whenever the sheet moves.
scripts/source-data/assessment.csv
